The crash is a global-buffer-overflow READ 1 in `fr_is_base16_nstd`. This reads `alphabet[(uint8_t)c]`. The alphabet is `fr_base16_alphabet_decode_mc[UINT8_MAX]` which is 256 bytes. So `alphabet[(uint8_t)c]` is always within bounds since `(uint8_t)c` is 0-255.

Wait, so the global-buffer-overflow READ 1 is reading `p[0]` or `p[1]` - reading past the end of the input buffer. The input buffer here is the argument value string.

